### Competitor URL & Analysis Summary
- **Supplied Competitor URL**: [https://www.caratlane.com/jewellery/bangles.html](https://www.caratlane.com/jewellery/bangles.html)
- **Structure & Gaps Identified**:
  - Competitor page is an e-commerce catalog/PLP showcasing ~261 bangle designs filtered by weight (2–5g, 5–10g, 10–20g, >30g), karatage (22Kt, 18Kt), and basic styles (daily wear, kada, cuff).
  - It lacks educational context on clasp mechanics, Indian bangle size conversions (inner diameter measurements in mm/inches vs 2-4, 2-6, 2-8), cultural silhouette histories (Sankha Pola, Pichodi, Valayal), and hallmarking verification.
- **Differentiation Strategy Executed**:
  - Crafted an authoritative 12-type design listicle with structural categorizations (continuous closed, hinged/openable, open/flexible), knuckle vs wrist measuring techniques, 22Kt vs 18Kt vs 14Kt durability insights, and styling guidelines without copying competitor wording or mentioning prices.

---

### Factual Sources & Hallmarking Standards
- **Bureau of Indian Standards (BIS)**: Mandatory 6-digit alphanumeric HUID (Hallmark Unique Identification) and 3-mark hallmarking compliance ([bis.gov.in](https://www.bis.gov.in/)).
- **World Gold Council (WGC)**: Purity standards for 22Kt (916), 18Kt (750), and 14Kt (585) ([gold.org](https://www.gold.org/)).
- **Indian Bangle Sizing Standard**: Inner diameter conversion formula (e.g. Size 2-4 = 2.25 inches / 57.2 mm; Size 2-6 = 2.375 inches / 60.3 mm).

